{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/0p7t8q","slideIndex":6,"text":"My best Transformer trained from scratch reached 16.6 percent pitch accuracy. With M2BERT and the context branch, I reached 64.9 percent—324 correct predictions out of 499. The correct pitch appears in the top five about 88 percent of the time.\n\nThe joint model reached 87.8 percent duration accuracy. The accidental model reached 87.7 percent on its separate set of 1,437 validation examples.\n\nMusic pretraining gave me the largest improvement. The context branch improved pitch further. Adding more training examples and unfreezing the backbone reduced accuracy, so I kept the earlier checkpoint.\n\nSources (not spoken)\nExperiment record: ml/correction_all_experiments.md\nCounts: context v3 pitch 324/499, top-5 439/499; joint duration 438/499; accidental v2 1260/1437."}
