{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/rjgjci","slideIndex":8,"text":"I solved three practical problems. Low pitch accuracy led me to pretrained M2BERT. A duration export bug led me to use quarter-note units consistently. For rare accidentals, I added 400 examples of double-flats and double-sharps. Macro F1 rose from 0.512 to 0.542, while overall accuracy fell slightly. That taught me to track both metrics.\n\nSources (not spoken)\nLocal records: ml/cleanup_summary.md; ml/data/runs/m2bert_acc_v2_20261102_115241/config.json"}
